### Problema 2.2:
Colector solar
triangular
**Enunciado:**
Triángulo
equilátero de:
$$1$$
$$\text{m}$$
de lado.
Vidrio (1):
$$\varepsilon_1 = 0,9$$
$$T_1 = 25$$
$$^{\circ}\text{C}$$
Placa (2):
$$\varepsilon_2 = 1$$
$$T_2 = 60$$
$$^{\circ}\text{C}$$
Placa (3):
$$\varepsilon_3 = 1$$
$$T_3 = 70$$
$$^{\circ}\text{C}$$
Calcule flujo
neto a la
cubierta.

**Resolución:**
**Paso 1:
Factores**
Por simetría:
$$F_{12} = F_{13} = 0,5$$

**Paso 2:
Calor**
$$E_{b1} = 447,1$$
$$\text{W/m}^2$$
$$E_{b2} = 698,0$$
$$\text{W/m}^2$$
$$E_{b3} = 787,0$$
$$\text{W/m}^2$$
$$R_{s1} = 0,1111$$
$$\text{m}^{-1}$$
$$R_{12} = 2,0$$
$$\text{m}^{-1}$$
$$R_{13} = 2,0$$
$$\text{m}^{-1}$$

Balance en J1:
$$\frac{E_{b1} - J_1}{R_{s1}} = \frac{J_1 - E_{b2}}{R_{12}} + \frac{J_1 - E_{b3}}{R_{13}}$$
$$J_1 = 476,64$$
$$\text{W/m}^2$$
$$q_1 = \frac{E_{b1} - J_1}{R_{s1}}$$
$$q_1 = -265,9$$
$$\text{W/m}$$
